null},{"t":"Is Right","img":null},{"t":"Is right","img":null},{"t":"Is right","img":null}],"ans":1,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv113c8v96bd"},{"test":"mv10t7l6ajsq","n":1791554223534,"type":"mcq","q":"","qImg":"content/media/9ea2a86156e79194.jpg","opts":[{"t":"Is right","img":null},{"t":"Is right","img":null},{"t":"Is right","img":null},{"t":"Is right","img":null}],"ans":1,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv114m4qy63u"},{"test":"mv10t7l6ajsq","n":1791554262897,"type":"mcq","q":"","qImg":"content/media/0bc9240e42596cef.jpg","opts":[{"t":"Is right","img":null},{"t":"Is right","img":null},{"t":"Is right","img":null},{"t":"Is right","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv115glnkpof"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791628354661,"type":"mcq","q":"All pure substances have:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"the same physical state","img":null},{"t":"Same colour","img":null},{"t":"Same composition","img":null},{"t":"Definite sets of properties","img":null}],"ans":3,"exp":"All pure substances have a definite set of properties. These properties include physical state, colour and composition, but they are not the same for all substances.\nPure substances can exist in different states - solid, liquid or gas. Different pure substances have different colours. Each pure substance has a fixed composition, but it is not the same as that of other substances.","expImg":null,"id":"mv299i06csl8"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791628483129,"type":"mcq","q":"Sugar is a compound which consists of the elements:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"C and H","img":null},{"t":"H and O","img":null},{"t":"C , H, O","img":null},{"t":"Hydrogen, Carbon, Sulphur","img":null}],"ans":2,"exp":"","expImg":"content/media/6a6bccb976339634.jpg","id":"mv29c99dqi6f"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791628626505,"type":"mcq","q":"Sulphur and Carbon are","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Metal","img":null},{"t":"Non metals","img":null},{"t":"Metalloids","img":null},{"t":"Mentals","img":null}],"ans":1,"exp":"Sulphur and carbon are non-metals with dull surfaces that do not shine unlike metals being lustrous. \nSulphur and carbon do not show metallic properties like conductivity or malleability. Metalloids have properties of both metals and non-metals (e.g., silicon). Noble gases (like helium, neon) are inert gases, unlike sulphur and carbon.","expImg":null,"id":"mv29fbrdloeo"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791628883441,"type":"mcq","q":"The most abundant elements in the universe are","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Neon and argon","img":null},{"t":"Hydrogen and helium","img":null},{"t":"Aluminium and copper","img":null},{"t":"Oxygen and nitrogen","img":null}],"ans":1,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv29ku0j7ygq"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791628936522,"type":"mcq","q":"The symbol of which of the following elements is derived from its Latin name ?","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Cobult","img":null},{"t":"Copper","img":null},{"t":"Calcium","img":null},{"t":"Chlorine","img":null}],"ans":1,"exp":"Among the following elements the symbol of copper i.e., Cu is derived from its latin name \"Cuprum\".","expImg":null,"id":"mv29lyyy1j3c"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791628993622,"type":"mcq","q":"The metal which is not a good conductor of electricity is:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Silver","img":null},{"t":"Aluminium","img":null},{"t":"Tungsten","img":null},{"t":"Copper","img":null}],"ans":2,"exp":"Metals are good conductors of electricity excepting tungsten, which is a poor conductor of electricity.\nSilver is the best conductor of electricity. Aluminium is a good conductor and commonly used in power cables. Copper is a very good conductor, widely used in wiring.","expImg":null,"id":"mv29n712zetn"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629017886,"type":"mcq","q":"Symbol of sodium","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"S","img":null},{"t":"N","img":null},{"t":"Na","img":null},{"t":"Sn","img":null}],"ans":2,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv29npr31kr3"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629185038,"type":"mcq","q":"","qImg":"content/media/3bcc464e212621cc.jpg","opts":[{"t":"(a)-(3), (b)-(4), (c)-(2), (d)-(5), (e)-(1)","img":null},{"t":"(a)-(3), (b)-(2), (c)-(4), (d)-(1), (e)-(5)","img":null},{"t":"(a)-(5), (b)-(4), (c)-(2), (d)-(3), (e)-(1)","img":null},{"t":"(a)-(1), (b)-(3), (c)-(5), (d)-(2), (e)-(4)","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv29raw87vkr"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629380450,"type":"mcq","q":"","qImg":"content/media/a8a615e86164fb4f.jpg","opts":[{"t":"Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.","img":null},{"t":"Both A and R are true and R is not the correct explanation of A.","img":null},{"t":"A true B false","img":null},{"t":"A false B true","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv29vhn4kz69"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629443386,"type":"mcq","q":"Brass and Bronze are","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Elements","img":null},{"t":"Compound","img":null},{"t":"Mixture","img":null},{"t":"None of these","img":null}],"ans":2,"exp":"Brass is a mixture of copper and zinc and bronze is a mixture of copper and tin.\nBrass and bronze are not single elements; they are made of more than one metal. So, they can't be elements. Compounds have a fixed chemical formula, but alloys do not.","expImg":null,"id":"mv29wu2izzio"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629473358,"type":"mcq","q":"The hardest naturally occurring substance is:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Graphite","img":null},{"t":"Iron","img":null},{"t":"Diamond","img":null},{"t":"Coal","img":null}],"ans":2,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv29xh73zaxw"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629516086,"type":"mcq","q":"Gold is used to make jewellery because it is","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Dull","img":null},{"t":"Malleable","img":null},{"t":"Ductile","img":null},{"t":"Lustrous and attractive","img":null}],"ans":3,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv29ye5z839y"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629567629,"type":"mcq","q":"A liquid non metal is","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Carbon","img":null},{"t":"Iron","img":null},{"t":"Bromine","img":null},{"t":"Boron","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv29zhxp8gnt"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629772893,"type":"mcq","q":"A mixture of mustard oil and water forms:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Compound","img":null},{"t":"An alloy","img":null},{"t":"Homogeneous mixture","img":null},{"t":"Heterogeneous mixture","img":null}],"ans":3,"exp":"Mustard oil and water are immiscible liquids. Their mixture is not uniformly distributed throughout. Hence, they form a heterogeneous mixture.","expImg":null,"id":"mv2a3wbi2gj2"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629836753,"type":"mcq","q":"A heterogeneous mixture is:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Made up of only one kind of atoms","img":null},{"t":"made up of only one kind of molecules","img":null},{"t":"made up of different kinds of atoms and molecules.","img":null},{"t":"one that looks uniform.","img":null}],"ans":2,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2a59ldbixj"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629871018,"type":"mcq","q":"An example of a homogeneous mixture is :","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Distilled water","img":null},{"t":"Sand water","img":null},{"t":"Sawdust and water","img":null},{"t":"Tap water","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2a60173uea"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629920306,"type":"mcq","q":"Which among the following is a set containing only mixtures ?","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"gold, common salt, water, alloy","img":null},{"t":"alloy, ink, honey, ice-cream","img":null},{"t":"milk, duralumin, brass, silver.","img":null},{"t":"alloy, mercury, air, sea water","img":null}],"ans":1,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2a722asngi"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629951207,"type":"mcq","q":"Copper is not a part of the alloy :","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"steel","img":null},{"t":"Brass","img":null},{"t":"Bronze","img":null},{"t":"Iron","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2a7pwn6fn1"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629989507,"type":"mcq","q":"Which of the following is not a mixture or impure substances?","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Distilled water","img":null},{"t":"Sugar solution","img":null},{"t":"Tap water","img":null},{"t":"Milk","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2a8jgk5wwq"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791630068339,"type":"mcq","q":"Alloys are which type of mixture","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Solid liquid","img":null},{"t":"Liquid liquid","img":null},{"t":"Solid gas","img":null},{"t":"Solid solid","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2aa8ac6t18"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791630135826,"type":"mcq","q":"The process of adding a chemical substance to help the suspended solid particles to deposit as sediment faster is called:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Sedimentation","img":null},{"t":"Loading","img":null},{"t":"Decantation","img":null},{"t":"Filtration","img":null}],"ans":1,"exp":"The process of helping fine solid particles in a solid-liquid mixture to settle faster, by adding a special chemical, is called loading or coagulation.\nSedimentation is the natural settling of particles at the bottom without adding any chemical. Decantation is the process of carefully pouring off the clear liquid after sedimentation. Filtration is the process of separating solids from liquids using a filter.","expImg":null,"id":"mv2abocy9uey"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791630171488,"type":"mcq","q":"Salt is separated from sea water by:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Evaporation","img":null},{"t":"Sublimation","img":null},{"t":"Magnetic separation","img":null},{"t":"Filtration","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2acfvl1jeu"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791630219556,"type":"mcq","q":"A gas dissolved in a liquid can be separated by:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Filtration","img":null},{"t":"Using magnet","img":null},{"t":"Sublimation","img":null},{"t":"Boiling","img":null}],"ans":3,"exp":"A mixture of gas in liquid can be separated by heating or boiling. Dissolved gas escapes from the liquid on heating or boiling.\nFiltration is used to separate insoluble solids from liquids, not dissolved gases. Magnet works only for magnetic materials like iron. Sublimation is used for solids that directly convert into gas, not for dissolved gases.","expImg":null,"id":"mv2adgyscw10"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791630260211,"type":"mcq","q":"Camphor can be separated from a mixture of sand and camphor by :","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Sublimation","img":null},{"t":"Filtration","img":null},{"t":"Winnowing","img":null},{"t":"Evaporation","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"Winnowing is used to separate lighter and heavier solids using air (like husk and grains), not suitable here.","expImg":null,"id":"mv2aecc3kiuy"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791630313585,"type":"mcq","q":"A separating funnel is used to separate","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Immiscible liquid","img":null},{"t":"Miscible liquid","img":null},{"t":"Sugar solution","img":null},{"t":"Chalk powder and water","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2afhipfm8w"}],"papers":[]}